<title>PERU: Peru net int'l reserves fall to $8.397 bln Nov 6.</title>
<headline>Peru net int'l reserves fall to $8.397 bln Nov 6.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's Central Reserve Bank said Monday its net international reserves fell to $8.397 billion on November 6 from $8.404 billion the week before.</p>
<p>The bank's foreign exchange position, or total liquidity minus short- and long-term debt obligations, was $1.603 billion on the same day.</p>
<p>International reserves ended 1995 at $6.641 billion.</p>
<p>-- Eduardo Orozco, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134</p>
